  "interventions": {
    "baseline": "Unmodified sustainable strategy with adaptive-mining variant, same half-day decisions and half-hour simulation.",
    "house16": "Only the first-three-houses order threshold changes from 22 logs to the actual 16-log cost; all actual costs/work/transport remain.",
    "fuel50-until-housed": "Target 50 before day36 while fewer than three houses are ordered; restore ordinary target once three are ordered or day36 begins. Construction is still ordinary.",
    "fuel0-first-year": "Negative control: fuel target0 from the opening through day47, including the entire first winter; restore ordinary target from day48. Initial 50 firewood is unchanged.",
    "cancel-for-stone": "Once only, d12–35, if an unhoused child exists, wood>=16, stone<8, and tree marks exist: cancel all tree marks and mark the nearest two path-verified stone deposits. All other ordinary rules remain."
  },
  "constraints": "No tracked-file edits, resource gifts, yield/cold/hunger/timing changes, manual worker assignments, instant buildings, or script replacement in the repository. Browser interaction and visual enjoyment are untested.",
  "interpretation": [
    "First-winter recovery is not a long-term safe strategy. Five-year failures and unchanged failure controls are deliberately retained.",
    "Earlier housing changes later births, random draws and construction routes, so do not assume equal action dates or attribute every later failure to one target value.",
    "Seeds49/54/55 baseline deaths are homeless-child exposure with positive firewood and zero unheated-home-days. They do not establish a missing housing control or universal housing-assignment defect.",
    "The cancellation result proves a conditional material reallocation, not a blanket cancel-all-orders cure.",
    "Historical playability/long_economy policies and their existing reports are unchanged."
  ],
